[{"id": "R013", "text": "They tap the bench, slide the screw back slightly, and let the stripped edge catch the new shape. They mark the new position with grease and leave the old screw visible beside the bench."}, {"id": "R014", "text": "They tap the screw with a thumbnail, lean the bench against the desk, and tap the stripped area again. When the screw remains bent, they move it closer to the bench and write the last line on a scrap before returning it to the bench."}, {"id": "R015", "text": "They press the screw head down and leave it for one minute as a check. They keep the bench open and avoid touching the head."}, {"id": "R016", "text": "They tap the bench, inspect the last strip, and keep the screw head spinning while stating that the screw goes into the bench and the whole thing is needed. They pull the bench aside and then return the screw head to it."}, {"id": "R017", "text": "They press the head back, then correct themselves when the screw is found missing and when the head is not. They move the bench, put it back, write the last piece, and keep the screw."}, {"id": "R018", "text": "They turn the screw between their fingers until the head catches the cloth. They leave the bench, put the screw beside it, and leave the clock face against the wall despite it having been wrong for some time."}, {"id": "R019", "text": "They place the screw head on the bench and wait for the last scrape without stating the outcome. They leave the head and screw beside each other and keep the job open."}, {"id": "R020", "text": "They turn the bench, mark the screw head with chalk, and run a thumb along the bench. They leave the head seated, mark the same spot again, test the screw with the other hand, and keep the bench still so the mark can be picked up."}, {"id": "R021", "text": "They tap the screw head, leave the bench, and turn the screw once."}, {"id": "R022", "text": "They tap the bench with their foot, lean against the head, and state that the screw stays. They write the last line beside it, tap the bench with a fingertip, and lean back, while the screw continues moving toward the edge."}, {"id": "R023", "text": "They return the bench, mark the last time with a thumb, and leave the bench when the screw head stays. They write the time on their palm, apologize, leave the screw in the bench, and keep the bench open while writing the time on their thumb."}, {"id": "R024", "text": "They press the screw head flat, leave the bench bare, and wait for the next movement. They keep the bench open for a minute and count the beats with a nail."}]
